cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Wer diese Arbeit verwendet, zitiert sie bitte wie folgt."
title: "Reformulation - Polykontexturale Logik in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  It has a new main part. Between Part A and Part B there stands a report, "What has
  become operational". It tells, by subject, in seven sections, what of Günther's and
  Kaehr's constructions stands here proved, executable and checkable: the coupling in
  Mahler's model, with Kaehr's distinction; Pfalzgraf's fibering; Kaehr's separating case
  and his calculus, Günther's implications as transjunctions, a bridge between two layers
  of the corpus, and the small figure with which Günther speaks three times. It ends with
  Günther's question, not with our answer.
  It says who checks. The voices that worked on this text are roles of instances of the
  same model family. They have found many errors in one another, and the list of errors
  shows it. Independent checkers they are not. Independent checks come from the proof
  environment, for the theorems, and from the author of the project. Whoever distrusts the
  marks, readings and quotations of this text is right to do so until a voice from outside
  has read them; a place for that is not yet set up.
type: software
